FloppyBridge RotationExtractor: a runtime overlap search window.

Applied to sources/src/floppybridge/ after the portability and latency patches
(neither touches RotationExtractor.* any more, so this is diffed against the
pristine donor files).

WHY

RotationExtractor will not declare a revolution ready until
OVERLAP_SEQUENCE_MATCHES * OVERLAP_EXTRA_BUFFER = 1024 * 6 = 6144 sequences have
arrived PAST the revolution point. 1024 of those are the overlap marker it
matches; the other 5120 are the +-search window getOverlapPosition() and
getTrueIndexPosition() sweep, sized for real-flux jitter and an arbitrary
anchor (the capture start, or the index pulse). At the ~5 us per sequence a DD
AmigaDOS track measures, that is ~30 ms of every buffered read.

A driver whose anchor is a sync word (AdmXCopyBufferedBridge, driver 5, anchors
48 cells past the first 0x4489 - docs/floppy-xcopy-buffered.md section 5) knows
its offset to within the pulse jitter (~70 sequences), so a 5120-sequence window
is ~70x more than it needs and the revolution can be declared that much sooner.

WHAT

- MFMExtractionTarget::setOverlapSearchWindow(sequences): a virtual with a no-op
  default, so a driver reaches it through BridgePLL::rotationExtractor() without
  RTTI. LinearExtractor keeps the no-op.
- RotationExtractor: m_overlapSearchWindow, default
  OVERLAP_SEQUENCE_MATCHES * (OVERLAP_EXTRA_BUFFER - 1) = 5120, clamped to
  [1, 5120]; overlapSequences() = marker + window. Every use of the fixed
  1024 * 6 (both search loops, the index-mode pre-index ring, both ready checks)
  now goes through those. The m_initialSequences allocation stays at the
  compile-time maximum, which the clamp never exceeds. Survives reset().
- MFMExtractionTarget::setOverlapMatches(sequences) / RotationExtractor::
  m_overlapMatches: the MARKER length, default OVERLAP_SEQUENCE_MATCHES = 1024,
  clamped to [64, 1024]. Both search loops, their thresholds and range checks
  use it; the IndexSequenceMarker array keeps its compile-time length and is
  always filled in full, only the first m_overlapMatches compared. Driver 5
  sets 256 (its anchor is inside a sector header, so 256 sequences are unique).

At the default the extractor is byte-for-byte the upstream behaviour, so the
Greaseweazle, DrawBridge and SuperCard Pro drivers are unchanged; only a driver
that calls the setter sees a difference. GreaseWeazleInterface's own 49 ms bound
(OVERLAP_SEQUENCE_MATCHES * OVERLAP_EXTRA_BUFFER * 8000 ns) is deliberately not
touched.

Build scripts: applied from BOTH scripts/build_puae.ps1 and scripts/build_puae.sh,
marker-guarded ("ADM: overlap search window" in RotationExtractor.h). Regenerated
with `git diff --no-index` from pre/post copies - the hunk counts are machine
made, not hand edited (docs/floppy-xcopy.md section 7 on why that matters).

